# Variable names a teammate may set for local Mishh Mashh runs. Names only: never commit values.
# Copy the lines you need into .env.local (git-ignored), uncomment them and add your value;
# `pnpm tools-dev` loads .env.local into the daemon.
# Every entry is optional. "Settings:" names the place in the app that takes the same value
# instead, so you can leave the line out here.

# --- Agency fast lane (QUICKSTART.md "Team setup" step 2) -----------------------------------
# Optional. Settings: Media providers -> Jev (TypeSafe).
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Optional. Settings: Media providers -> DeepSeek (fast lane).
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Optional. Settings: Media providers -> Cerebras (fast lane).
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# --- Media providers (one name per provider in apps/daemon/src/media/config.ts) -------------
# Optional. Settings: Media providers.
# OD_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Settings: Media providers.
# OD_TAVILY_API_KEY=

# --- Runtime -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. The daemon data root; read root AGENTS.md "Daemon data directory contract" first.
# Set it here or in the shell, not both with different values: tools-dev takes this file's value,
# and `sh scripts/team-setup.sh` stops when they disagree. No Settings equivalent.
# OD_DATA_DIR=
# Optional. A Chromium-based browser outside the standard locations. No Settings equivalent.
# OD_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=
# Optional. Where `od` finds the daemon when it cannot discover it. No Settings equivalent.
# OD_DAEMON_URL=

# --- Team setup report ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Comma-separated design-system ids the team expects installed; setup reports each
# one that is missing or still a draft. Export it in the shell before running setup (the setup
# report does not read .env.local). No Settings equivalent.
# OD_SETUP_EXPECTED_KITS=
